{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-141133-r4531806","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Arjoli (Maltese Herbed Bread Dip)","sourcePageId":141133,"sourceRevision":"4531806","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-08-21T00:56:06Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Arjoli%20(Maltese%20Herbed%20Bread%20Dip)&oldid=4531806","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:22:53.744Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Mediterranean recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for dip","Category:Recipes using anchovy","Category:Recipes using anchovy paste","Category:Recipes using caper","Category:Recipes using garlic","Category:Recipes using mint","Category:Recipes using olive","Category:Recipes without servings","Category:Very Easy recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"4bdbf483b3b5ca861cda52e70d395c37bddb628460228ff156106c13313d067c","sourceWikitext":"__NOTOC__{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Sauce recipes\n| Time = 1 day\n| Difficulty = 1\n}}\n\n{{recipe}}\n\n'''Arjoli''' (alternately spelled Ajjoli) is a Maltese dip or spread. It is typically held together with bread.\n\n==Ingredients==\n* 2 packets Maltese ''galletti'' (round hard Ship's Biscuit)\n* Fresh [[Cookbook:Basil|Basil]], [[Cookbook:Mincing|minced]]\n* Fresh [[Cookbook:Mint|mint]], minced\n* Fresh [[Cookbook:Parsley|parsley]], minced\n*4 cloves [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]], [[Cookbook:Dice|diced]]\n* [[Cookbook:Olive|Olives]] (black and green), diced\n* [[Cookbook:Caper|Capers]], [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]]\n*[[Cookbook:Anchovy paste|Anchovy paste]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Tomato Paste|tomato paste]] (kunserva)\n\n==Procedure==\n# Let the galletti soak in water overnight to soften.\n# Combine soaked galletti and all remaining ingredients in a mortar and pestle. Crush to a paste consistency.\n\n==Notes, tips, and variations==\n* Use dry Maltese bread instead of the galletti.\n* Add one or two sun-dried [[Cookbook:Tomato|tomatoes]] for a spicy taste.\n* Another Maltese version of Ajjoli (alternative spelling) mixes lots of diced tomato flesh (no skin or seeds) with very finely diced garlic and plenty of olive oil which should be left for flavors to blend for at least an hour.\n\n[[Category:Mediterranean recipes|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes using olive|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garlic|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes for dip|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes using anchovy]]\n[[Category:Recipes using anchovy paste]]\n[[Category:Recipes using caper]]\n[[Category:Recipes using mint]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Arjoli (Maltese Herbed Bread Dip)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"2 packets Maltese galletti (round hard Ship's Biscuit)","sourceText":"2 packets Maltese galletti (round hard Ship's Biscuit)","amountText":"2 packets Maltese galletti (round hard Ship's Biscuit)","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"Fresh Basil, minced","sourceText":"Fresh Basil, minced","amountText":"Fresh Basil, minced","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"Fresh mint, minced","sourceText":"Fresh mint, minced","amountText":"Fresh mint, minced","amount"